# Read n numbers and print them in reverse order. The numbers are kept in
# the cells 100, 101, ...; i holds the address of the one in hand.

π' → A
? → n
100 → i
100 + n → e

π' → B              # Read while i < e.
(1 ∩ (e ∸ i))·C + (1 ∸ (e ∸ i))·D → π

π' → C
? → ↓i
i + 1 → i
B → π

π' → D              # Print while i > 100.
(1 ∩ (i ∸ 100))·E → π

π' → E
i ∸ 1 → i
↓i → ?
D → π
